license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. Over a perfect henselian subfield of the Hahn field k((y^Q)) containing k(y) and without finite accumulation points, a finite Artin-Schreier tower of depth one is a compositum of Artin-Schreier extensions. This is the converse conjectured by Nart and Novacoski. The converse is formalized in Lean for towers in the Hahn field with depth one expressed through Okutsu sequences. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
